 "about": "The normalizer of the textedit world (specification section 14): deterministic rules applied to a command before the textedit reader, in Python (training/worlds/textedit/normalize.py, used by the generator) and in JavaScript (app/src/text/textnorm.js, used by the editor), from this one table. Order: quoted strings become one token (lower-case, spaces -> '_'), remembered with their original text; lower-case; contractions; punctuation split; multi-word expressions (longest first); single-word synonyms; number words to digits ('one' never); verb forms (a format word with no world verb before it is the verb: 'bold the last word' -> 'embolden the last word'); after a match-intro word ('word', 'words', 'phrase') the next token is remembered as a piece of text. The 'dictation' block is NOT applied to commands: it is the spoken punctuation and layout table of dictation mode (spec 14.2), applied to content by app/src/text/dictation.js.",
